g Touchdowns","Long Rushing"],"groups":[{"title":"Passing","count":10},{"title":"Rushing","count":5}],"games":[{"id":"401858432","date":"2026-09-05","week":1,"type":"reg","home":true,"opp":"BALL","oppName":"Ball State Cardinals","result":"W","score":"56-3","values":[21,25,320,84,3,0,48,2,231.1,96.8,3,-9,-3,1,3]},{"id":"401856682","date":"2026-09-12","week":2,"type":"reg","home":false,"opp":"TEX","oppName":"Texas Longhorns","result":"L","score":"24-23","values":[17,32,278,53.1,1,1,43,2,130.2,90.4,4,-7,-1.8,0,5]},{"id":"401858454","date":"2026-09-19","week":3,"type":"reg","home":true,"opp":"KENT","oppName":"Kent State Golden Flashes","result":"W","score":"59-3","values":[18,22,241,81.8,2,0,49,1,203.8,73.9,2,-6,-3,0,1]},{"id":"401858465","date":"2026-09-26","week":4,"type":"reg","home":true,"opp":"ILL","oppName":"Illinois Fighting Illini","result":"W","score":"42-19","values":[27,36,367,75,4,0,72,0,197.3,95.4,7,29,4.1,1,8]},{"id":"401858473","date":"2026-10-03","week":5,"type":"reg","home":false,"opp":"IOWA","oppName":"Iowa Hawkeyes","result":"W","score":"31-14","values":[20,27,324,74.1,3,0,57,4,211.5,89.6,9,-1,-0.1,0,9]},{"id":"401858483","date":"2026-10-10","week":6,"type":"reg","home":true,"opp":"MD","oppName":"Maryland Terrapins","result":"W","score":"45-16","values":[13,21,242,61.9,4,1,68,2,212,44.4,7,11,1.6,0,8]},{"id":"401858488","date":"2026-10-17","week":7,"type":"reg","home":false,"opp":"IU","oppName":"Indiana Hoosiers","result":"W","score":"19-15","values":[15,29,235,51.7,2,2,38,3,128.7,68.1,5,-26,-5.2,0,5]}]}},"summaryLabel":"2026 season stats","news":[{"headline":"Betting on Ohio State-USC: How the Trojans can pull off the upset","description":"Could USC give the Buckeyes a good scare on Halloween? Let's dive into the numbers to find the best betting angle.","published":"2026-10-28T13:44:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50300744/college-football-betting-odds-week-9-ohio-state-usc-upset","type":"Story","byline":"Pamela Maldonado","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ryan Day: Ohio State planning to be without QB Julian Sayin through postseason","description":"Buckeyes coach Ryan Day declined to put a timeline on Julian Sayin's recovery but said they are planning to move forward without him through the rest of the year.","published":"2026-10-21T15:55:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50232936/ohio-state-plans-julian-sayin-rest-season","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ohio State QB Julian Sayin out 'several weeks' with shoulder injury","description":"Ohio State's Julian Sayin will miss \"several weeks\" with an injury to his throwing shoulder, coach Ryan Day said Saturday after his team escaped with a 19-15 victory at No. 5 Indiana, a game in which Luke Fahey finished up as the Buckeyes' quarterback.","published":"2026-10-17T22:26:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50204305/julian-sayin-several-weeks-ohio-state-ryan-day-says","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 NFL draft QB rankings: Arch Manning, Dante Moore, Drew Mestemaker in top 15","description":"Who are the best quarterbacks in the 2027 draft class? We sized up the top 15, including Arch Manning, Dante Moore, Trinidad Chambliss and Darian Mensah.","published":"2026-10-09T12:14:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/50117790/2027-nfl-draft-quarterbacks-ranking-strengths-weaknesses","type":"Story","byline":"Jordan Reid","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ohio State rolls past Iowa behind big games from Sayin, Smith","description":"Julian Sayin threw for 324 yards and three touchdowns, two to Jeremiah Smith, and No. 5 Ohio State beat No. 14 Iowa 31-14 on Saturday.","published":"2026-10-04T02:48:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50094266/ohio-state-rolls-iowa-big-games-sayin-smith","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5079712/julian-sayin","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julian_Sayin"},"pick":{"pick":57,"round":2,"team":"KC","provisional":true},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Julian Sayin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julian_Sayin","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-17T20:09:17Z","intro":"Julian Sayin (SAY-ən; born July 22, 2005) is an American college football quarterback for the Ohio State Buckeyes.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Sayin grew up in Carlsbad, California and attended Carlsbad High School in Carlsbad.\n\nSayin was rated a five-star recruit and the second-best quarterback prospect in the 2024 class. He received his first scholarship offer when he was in 8th grade from Kenny Dillingham, then the offensive coordinator at Florida State. Sayin committed to play college football at Alabama during his junior season after considering offers from Georgia and LSU. He had other notable offers from Notre Dame, Texas, and Florida."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"ALABAMA\nSayin began practicing as an early enrollee with Alabama during the 2023 season in preparation for the 2024 Rose Bowl. On January 19, 2024, Sayin entered the transfer portal following the retirement of Nick Saban.\n\n\n2024 SEASON\nOn January 21, 2024, Sayin announced he was transferring to Ohio State. On January 31, he signed a name, image, and likeness (NIL) deal with Panini America, a trading card company owned by Panini Group. On February 14, 2024, Sayin signed another NIL deal this time with an Ohio State-driven collective known as The Foundation. Sayin threw his first collegiate touchdown against Western Michigan on September 7, 2024. Sayin made a few more appearances throughout the season, and was part of the 2025 College Football Playoff National Championship team.\n\n2025 SEASON\nOn August 18, 2025, Sayin was named the starting quarterback by head coach Ryan Day as a redshirt freshman following the departure of Will Howard to the 2025 NFL Draft. In his first start, Sayin led the Buckeyes to a 14–7 victory over No. 1 Texas, completing 13 of 20 passes for 126 yards and one touchdown. The following week, he went 18 of 19 for 306 yards with four touchdowns and one interception in a 70–0 win against Grambling State. In a Week 8 victory against Wisconsin, Sayin completed 36 of 42 passes for a career-high 393 yards and four touchdowns. He led the Buckeyes to an undefeated 12–0 regular season, earning a No. 1 national ranking and a berth in the 2025 Big Ten Football Championship Game against Indiana. Sayin completed 21 of 29 passes for 258 yards with one touchdown and one interception in a 13–10 loss. In the CFP quarterfinal at the Cotton Bowl, Sayin and Ohio State were defeated by Miami, 24–14. He finished the game 22 of 35 for 287 yards with one touchdown and two interceptions.\nSayin concluded the season with 301 completions on 391 attempts (77.0% completion rate, third-best all-time in FBS) for 3,610 yards, 32 touchdowns, and eight interceptions. He was named Second-Team All-Big Ten and received both the Shaun Alexander Freshman of the Year and Big Ten Freshman of the Year honors. He also finished fourth in Heisman Trophy voting.\nIn his 2025 full-season campaign, Sayin fell short of breaking Bo Nix's NCAA pass completion percentage record set in 2023, finishing at 77.0% to Nix's 77.5%. Sayin was on pace to break the record, but was derailed by a poor performance during a losing effort to Miami in the 2025 Cotton Bowl Classic where he completed just 22 of 35 passes with 2 interceptions, falling just two missed completions shy of Nix's record."}]}}